U2W iap2-wait: /dev/ipod_iap2 without busy polling.

- open() waits up to 200 ms for the host to select the iPod HID alt setting before the same
  -ENODEV: fakeiOSDevice retries open() in a ~10 ms loop for 300 s when no car is attached
  (bench, charger), which cost ~28% CPU (strace 2026-10-19: 47 Hz, each re-parsing
  /tmp/.riddle.conf); now ~5 Hz.
- read() and write() sleep on a wait queue instead of msleep(5) polls (up to 5 ms extra
  latency per iAP2 message and constant wakeups).
- iap2_lock becomes a spinlock: f_hid_set_report_complete() runs in the UDC hard-IRQ
  completion and must not take a mutex; read() copies out through a bounce buffer.

